    "in a text with no spaces between words.",
    "`joins`: a word the person sets two clauses apart with. `intent`: what says a line is done, dropped, cancelled or changed.",
    "`common`: words that carry no content, so two texts sharing only these are not about the same thing.",
    "`about`: words are about a line when they share at least `share` of its content words (never fewer than `least`); two words",
    "are one when either begins with the other and the shorter has `stem` letters. A message is read whole: no count of its clauses is cut.",
    "An answer to a question: `nays` are the negations that answer by themselves (a clause of only these negates no clause after",
    "it); `assent` says yes and `picks` point at what the question offered, so an answer of only these takes its value from the",
    "question's words. `held`: a value is the answer's when at most `foreign` of its words, and at most `share` of them, are not.",
    "`takesAll`: what says the person takes whole what was offered to them (every proposal shown, the defaults); what was shown is",
    "the caller's to know, and a sentence with a negation never takes anything.",
    "`aside`: the words for setting work aside; a question of the AI that holds one asks the person exactly that."
